ed (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.linkId (linkId)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.linkId</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.linkId` has a context of ResearchStudy.arm based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.linkId` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.intendedExposure (intendedExposure)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.intendedExposure</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.intendedExposure` has a context of ResearchStudy.arm based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.intendedExposure` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.observedGroup (observedGroup)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.observedGroup</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.observedGroup` has a context of ResearchStudy.arm based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.comparisonGroup.observedGroup` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.objective.description (description)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.objective.description</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.objective.description` has a context of ResearchStudy.objective based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.objective.description` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure (outcomeMeasure)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure` has a context of ResearchStudy based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nA study may have multiple distinct outcome measures that can be used to assess the overall goal for a study. The goal of a study is in the objective whereas the metric by which the goal is assessed is the outcomeMeasure. Examples: Time to Local Recurrence (TLR), Disease-free Survival (DFS), 30 Day Mortality, Systolic BP</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.name (name)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure:name</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.name` is part of an existing definition because parent element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.name` has a context of ResearchStudy based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.name` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.type (type)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure:type</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.type` is part of an existing definition because parent element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.type` has a context of ResearchStudy based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.type` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.description (description)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure:description</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.description` is part of an existing definition because parent element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.description` has a context of ResearchStudy based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.description` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.reference (reference)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure:reference</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.reference` is part of an existing definition because parent element `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure` requires a cross-version extension.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.reference` has a context of ResearchStudy based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.outcomeMeasure.reference` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.result (result)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/5.0/StructureDefinition/extension-ResearchStudy.result</td><td>Element `ResearchStudy.result` has a context of ResearchStudy based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `ResearchStudy`.\nElement `ResearchStudy.result` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).</td></tr></table><hr/><p><b>Group 3 </b>Mapping from <code>http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/ResearchStudy|5.0.0</code> to <a href=\"http://hl7.org/fhir/extensions/5.2.0/index.html\">FHIR Extensions Packversion: 5.2.0)</a></p><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Source Code</b></td><td><b>Relationship</b></td><td><b>Target Code</b></td><td><b>Comment</b></td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.site (site)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#equivalent\" title=\"equivalent\">is equivalent to</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/alternate-reference</td><td>R5: additional references</td></tr><tr><td>ResearchStudy.recruitment.eligibility (eligibility)</td><td><a href=\"CodeSystem-concept-map-relationship.html#wider\" title=\"wider\">maps to wider concept</a></td><td>http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/alternate-reference</td><td>R5: additional references</td></tr></table></div>"^^rdf:XMLLiteral ]
